{
  "name": "encoding-reflection-template-names-an-unwritten-field",
  "description": "A template execution reads each field an action of its templates names, whether or not anything writes it, because executing an action that names a field the type lacks fails. An action that prints a value prints it through fmt, so every field the formatting walk reaches is read, exported or not, written or not: the argument printed by {{.}} or by printf, a field printed whole, each element a range binds, the value a with binds, a variable's value and the dot a defined template is invoked with. Dot is typed as the engine binds it. An action whose value has no one static type that is no interface, as for a method or template function result, an interface-typed field or a reflect.Value argument, reads only what an action of a template the analysis does not read reads. A field no action names and nothing writes, or that is written and never read, is reported.",
  "languages": ["go"],
  "target_kind": "application",
